# PostgREST (`postgrest-postgrest`)

Transform your PostgreSQL database into a high-performance RESTful API with PostgREST. Enjoy rapid response times, enhanced security, and seamless scaling for robust, efficient app development.

[Service documentation](https://docs.osaas.io/osaas.wiki/Service%3A-PostgREST.html) · [Source](https://github.com/PostgREST/postgrest)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "postgrest-postgrest"
  name       = "mypostgrest"

  parameters = {
    # DbAnonRole = "..."
    # DbSchemas  = "..."
  }

  sensitive_parameters = {
    DbUri = var.db_uri
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `DbUri` | string | yes | PostgreSQL connection string PostgREST uses to reach the database (upstream PGRST_DB_URI), e.g. postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname. Not reloadable at runtime. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |
| `DbAnonRole` | string | no | Database role PostgREST switches to for requests without a valid JWT (upstream PGRST_DB_ANON_ROLE). It is the permission boundary for unauthenticated clients: they can only do what GRANTs on this role allow, so give it minimal privileges; if unset, anonymous access is blocked. |
| `DbSchemas` | string | no | Comma-separated list of database schemas exposed through the REST API (upstream PGRST_DB_SCHEMAS, default 'public'), e.g. public,api. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
